The project will be divided into five phases: Framing, Design, Pilot, Generalisation, and Run. Each phase will end with a formal review and a go/no-go decision.

In the Framing phase, we will define the project scope, goals, and deliverables. This phase will last for two weeks and will require our project director, solution architect, and one engineer.

The Design phase will focus on designing the AI assistance solution, including the integration with existing hospital information systems and electronic patient records. This phase will also last for two weeks and will require our solution architect, two engineers, and our data scientist.

In the Pilot phase, we will deploy the AI assistance solution to a limited perimeter of one or two departments and test its functionality and effectiveness. This phase will last for three months and will require our project director, solution architect, two engineers, and our security compliance lead.

The Generalisation phase will involve deploying the AI assistance solution to all services and ensuring its integration with existing systems. This phase will last for six months and will require our entire dedicated team, including our project director, solution architect, two engineers, data scientist, and security compliance lead.

Finally, in the Run phase, we will ensure the continuous operation of the AI assistance solution and provide maintenance and support services. This phase will last for two years and will require our project director, one engineer, and our security compliance lead.

Throughout the project, we will have a joint steering committee with the client, meeting monthly, and an operational committee meeting fortnightly. We will also maintain a RACI matrix to ensure clear roles and responsibilities.

Our available capacity includes a dedicated team with a project director, solution architect, two engineers, one data scientist, and a shared security compliance lead. We also have additional resources for change management and training.

We will allocate our resources according to the phase requirements, ensuring that we have the necessary expertise and capacity to deliver each phase's objectives. Our timeline is estimated to be around 24 months, with the following milestones: 

- Month 1-2: Framing phase
- Month 3-4: Design phase
- Month 5-8: Pilot phase
- Month 9-14: Generalisation phase
- Month 15-26: Run phase

We will ensure that our solution complies with regulatory requirements such as GDPR and ensures data sovereignty by hosting the solution on a French sovereign cloud provider, OuraneCloud, which is SecNumCloud-qualified and HDS-certified. We will also rely on our partnership with Ligeo Santé for health-IT integration and FHIR/INS interoperability work.

Our approach will guarantee the expected quality of service, ensure continuity of care, and reduce complexity of procedures while improving efficiency and quality of care.
